#
# Typographical conventions of the grammar notation; nothing is observable.

assertion  XCU.1.3-grammar-conventions.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.3/special grammar notation
class      untestable
since      1992
says       The grammar notation of the standard is a way of describing syntax;
           the syntax each utility accepts is what its own module checks.
reason     The notation is a means of presentation; the syntax it describes is
           checked in the modules of the utilities and the shell language.
